From 8d3126a1b198ba4bd50e3b695640f3631a769cad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:54:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/57] hw/misc: EVSYS model, event routing between PIC32CM
 peripherals

EVSYS U2256: channels route a generator or a software event to the
users that select them, on the synchronous, resynchronized and
asynchronous paths; CHSTATUS, OVR and EVD follow PIC32CM MC00 silicon
(firmware/hello/tests/evprobe.c): the clocked paths need the channel's
generic clock, an event with a user not ready is lost with OVR, one
with no user sets OVR and CHBUSY, a pulse seen on both edges sets OVR,
USER.CHANNEL keeps 4 bits.

The generated device descriptor gains the ATDF event table, and the SoC
wires event SIG[n] of an instance to its "sig-event" output or
"sig-event-in" input. Event outputs: EIC (level senses as levels, as
on silicon), TC, RTC (PERn, CMPn, OVF). Event inputs: TC (COUNT,
RETRIGGER, START, TCINV; ready while enabled) and PORT (OUT, SET, CLR,
TGL; an OUT action with a pulse leaves OUT unchanged). New qtest
pic32cm-evsys-test.

Peripheral Pretender: a personal project; not for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
